message: "If you use or reference this research monograph or dataset, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Comparative Anthropological History of World Religions, Trans-Ethnic Mystical Invariants, and Predictive Game-Theoretic Historiography"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Andre"
    affiliation: "NorthStar Prime Research & Publishing Institute"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://northstarprime.net/literature/"
abstract: >-
  This five-part humanities working-paper series examines the evolutionary anthropology of human ritual and religious systems from Upper Paleolithic shamanic complexes and Neolithic agricultural pantheons through the Axial Age transformations (Vedic/Upanishadic, Buddhist, Daoist, Confucian, Zoroastrian, Abrahamic, and Indigenous traditions), paired with formal game-theoretic modeling of institutional cooperation, elite overproduction, and strategic equilibrium transitions in historical civilizations.
keywords:
  - "anthropology of religion"
  - "comparative mythology"
  - "Axial Age"
  - "game theory"
  - "predictive historiography"
  - "contemplative traditions"
